// Prisma schema — the single source of truth for the database shape.
//
// It is deliberately empty of models. TAR-38's ADR picks Prisma; TAR-42 (this
// file) wires up the local runner; **TAR-39 owns the data model** and adds the
// first entities, along with the tenant-scoping mechanism (RLS session variable
// or a query-level guard). Adding speculative models here would pre-empt that
// decision.
//
// The connection URL lives in `prisma.config.mjs`, not here: Prisma 7 reads the
// datasource URL from the config file and no longer loads `.env` on its own.
//
// No `generator` block yet, so no client is generated and `@prisma/client` is
// not a dependency. The story that writes the first query adds both — Prisma 7
// clients need a driver adapter, which is a choice for whoever writes that code.

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}
